---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout title="Automating PO Lifecycle Tracking From Issue to Delivery - Marker">
  <Navbar />
  <main id="main-content">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-16 md:pt-24 md:pb-24">
      <a href="/case-studies" class="mb-8 inline-flex items-center text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">
        <svg class="mr-1 h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path>
        </svg>
        All Case Studies
      </a>

      <span class="mb-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">DTC Furniture</span>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Automating PO Lifecycle Tracking From Issue to Delivery</h1>

      <div class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted/50 p-5 text-sm">
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Company</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">Direct-to-consumer furniture brand with complex production milestones and varied payment terms across vendors</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Team</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">Sourcing team managing PO lifecycle from issue through production, QC, shipping, and final delivery</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Key Challenge</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">No centralized view of where each PO stood in its lifecycle; WIP status and QC milestones tracked manually through scattered conversations</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Challenge</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">A sourcing leader at this DTC furniture brand managed purchase orders through a lifecycle that was significantly more complex than apparel: from PO issue through material procurement, production stages (including "whitewood" milestones specific to furniture), quality checks, packaging, shipping, and final delivery. Each stage had its own communication patterns, often with different contacts at the factory.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Tracking WIP (work-in-progress) status meant asking factories directly: "Have they finished whitewood? Has it gone to finishing? When does QC happen?" These questions were sent via email and WhatsApp, and the answers arrived at unpredictable intervals. With dozens of POs active at any time, each at a different stage, the sourcing team had no centralized view of where things stood. They described the process of getting products into the QC tracking system as "impossible" given current bandwidth.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Payment terms added further complexity: some vendors wouldn't ship until paid, others didn't require payment until after delivery, and terms varied by supplier and sometimes by order. Missing a payment deadline could hold up an entire shipment.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Approach</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Marker tracks each PO through its full lifecycle by extracting status updates from supplier communication. When a factory confirms that whitewood is complete, or sends photos from a QC inspection, or provides a shipping notification, Marker updates the PO's status automatically. The sourcing team sees a dashboard of all active POs with their current stage — without needing to ask factories for updates or manually update a tracking spreadsheet.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">For milestones where the team expects an update and hasn't received one, Marker sends automated reminder emails to the supplier. Payment term deadlines are tracked per PO and per vendor, with alerts before a payment is due — especially critical for vendors who hold shipments pending payment. The result is a continuous, communication-driven view of the PO lifecycle that replaces the manual WIP tracking that consumed the team's time.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">Key Takeaways</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-muted-foreground">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>PO status updated automatically from supplier communication — production milestones, QC updates, and shipping confirmations</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Automated supplier reminders when expected milestone updates haven't been received</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Payment term deadlines tracked per PO and per vendor, with alerts before due dates</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Dashboard view of all active POs by lifecycle stage, replacing manual WIP tracking</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12 rounded-lg border border-primary/20 bg-primary/5 p-6 text-center">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-foreground">See how Marker automates PO lifecycle tracking from issue to delivery.</p>
        <a href="/book-demo" class="mt-4 inline-flex h-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-primary px-6 text-sm font-medium text-primary-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-primary/90 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2">Book a Demo</a>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
